WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.550
A paint factory sits at
the edge of a busy town.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:06.710
Each batch it sells
brings in money and jobs.

3
00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:08.250
Buyers want the paint.

4
00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:09.810
Workers want the jobs.

5
00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:12.270
So surely, the more the factory makes,

6
00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:16.070
the better? Yet economists
warn that markets can make

7
00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.830
too much of some things,

8
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.740
and too little of others.

9
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.600
So why might a busy
factory make more than is

10
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.950
best for the people who live around it?

11
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.460
In this mission, you'll sort
four kinds of externality,

12
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.090
from factory smoke to vaccination.

13
00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.480
Then you'll run a smoky factory:

14
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.960
slide one number and watch
how many batches it makes.

15
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.440
Your mission: find out when
making more leaves the people

16
00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.370
around a factory worse off.
